I propose a capacity-driven proactive opening strategy combined with dynamic maintenance-wave scheduling. The rule opens a new robot as soon as the estimated remaining capacity is insufficient, choosing a type that keeps the required concurrency low and prefers already-opened types. For robot selection, it switches between a “prep” mode (when active robots exceed the required concurrency) that pushes the most-used robot toward maintenance, a “conserve” mode during maintenance that protects robots with high remaining budgets, and a balanced mode otherwise.

