The rule uses a maintenance-wave idea: when no robot is already down, it deliberately pushes the most-used available robot toward its maintenance limit to stagger maintenance events; while a robot is down, it protects fresh robots by preferring high remaining budget and rotates fairly among them. The remaining reuse alternatives are ordered by fairness so genome deviations can trade resources against balance.

