The improved rule keeps the count/hour balance but makes maintenance handling horizon-aware: it only rushes a robot with one duty left into maintenance when that robot can return before the horizon (and no other robot is already in maintenance), while near the end it avoids triggering unnecessary maintenance. New-robot type choice now accounts for whether the horizon is short enough that maintenance will never be reached, instead of always amortizing maintenance time.

